@startuml
title SFTP Filesystem & Byte Channel States\n(NfsSftpFsProvider / NfsSyncingByteChannel)

[*] --> Unbound : provider created

state Unbound {
  Unbound : do / await mount request;\nno connection established
}

state Mounted {
  Mounted : entry / auth env var resolved;\nremote root verified via one-off SFTP check
  Mounted : do / accept file operations;\neach opens a short-lived SFTP session,\ncompletes the work, then disconnects
  Mounted : exit / flush any open byte channels
}

state Error {
  Error : entry / record failure cause
  Error : do / await retry or dismiss
}

Unbound --> Mounted : newFileSystem()\n[auth env var present;\nremote root reachable]
Unbound --> Error   : newFileSystem()\n[auth env var missing\nor connection refused]
Mounted --> Unbound : close()
Mounted --> Error   : I/O failure during operation
Error   --> Unbound : retry / dismiss
Error   --> [*]     : fatal error / app exit
Unbound --> [*]     : filesystem closed

note right of Mounted
  No persistent TCP connection is maintained.
  Each file operation (list, stat, read, write,
  delete, rename) opens a fresh SSH/SFTP session
  per call and disconnects in a finally block.
end note

state "Byte Channel (one per open file)" as BC {
  [*] --> Open
  Open : entry / remote file content pre-loaded\ninto an in-memory byte buffer
  Open : do / reads and writes update the\nbuffer in memory; position tracked
  Open --> Flushing : close() [dirty]
  Open --> [*]      : close() [clean — no remote write needed]
  Flushing : do / write buffer to remote\nvia a new short-lived SFTP session
  Flushing --> [*]  : flush complete
}

note right of BC
  NfsSyncingByteChannel buffers file content
  in memory. Remote I/O happens only once,
  on close(), when the buffer has been modified.
end note
@enduml
